{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface","excerpts":[["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:257-weighted","A weighted summability criterion","<p><em>\nLet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> be an integer, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi></mrow></math></span> be a finite nonempty set of\nprimes, and let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span> be infinite. Write </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em>\nwhere <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is the exponent of\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi></math></span> in <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></span>; thus <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is the <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi></mrow></math></span>-part of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></span>. If </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>1</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> is\nirrational. More precisely, for </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span> there is an <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#prop:257-finite-witness-rule","realising finite monotone witness\nrules","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi></math></span> be a finite set\nof primes, and let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒰</mi></mrow></math></span> be an\nupward-closed family of subsets of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒰</mi></mrow></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>∅</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>𝒰</mi></mrow></math></span>. There is a\nset <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span> with <span class=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span> such that, for every integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and every finite set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi></mrow></math></span> of primes, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>12</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒰</mi></mrow><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Moreover <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is irrational for every infinite\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></math></span> and every\ninteger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:257-variable-fractional-cover","A summable family of divisor majorants","<p><em> For each <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span> be finite,\nlet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> satisfy </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span>. If </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>14</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>j</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> then <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nis irrational for every infinite <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><munder><mo>⋃</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> and every integer\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:257-mixed-supports","mixed weighted and cover supports","<p><em>\nLet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>.\nSuppose <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi></math></span> has finite weighted mass\n<a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#eq:257-weighted-mass\">(1)</a> at\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> for a finite nonempty prime set\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒫</mi></mrow></math></span>. Suppose also that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>V</mi><mo>⊆</mo><munder><mo>⋃</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> for sets and\nmajorants satisfying Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#thm:257-variable-fractional-cover\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:257-variable-fractional-cover\">1.3</a>,\nwith <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#eq:257-strengthened-cover\">(14)</a> or its\npositive-weight variant. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is irrational for every infinite\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>V</mi></math></span> and every\ninteger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:geometry","Achievement-set geometry","<p><em> <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span> is compact, closed, perfect,\ntotally disconnected and nowhere dense, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>volume</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>.\nThus its measure is positive although it contains no interval. Its\nconvex hull is <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span>, where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>. The positive-index\ndigit coding onto <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span> is\ninjective: each achievable real has <em>exactly one</em>\nsupport.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:supported-dichotomy","Support-restricted refinement","<p><em> Use\nzero-based indices in this statement: coordinate <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> carries weight <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>. For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span>, consider the sums\nthat use only coordinates in <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi></math></span>. If\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>J</mi></math></span> is\nfinite, this achievement set has measure <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow></msup></math></span>; if\ninfinitely many coordinates are omitted, its measure is zero.\nInjectivity survives every restriction; perfectness is proved when <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi></math></span> is infinite. No perfectness claim is\nmade for finite <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi></math></span>, whose coding\nrange is finite.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:greedy-survival","Membership equals greedy survival; the\nfatal-gap dichotomy","<p><em> For a real target <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> be the remainder after the greedy\nrule has processed weights <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>, and let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span>, with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi></math></span>. Then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext> and </mtext><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mtext> </mtext><mtext>for every </mtext><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span>, nonmembership is\nequivalent to a finite strict gap between the two next-prefix intervals;\nsee Observation <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#obs:general-target-gap\">9.44</a>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#prop:canon","Uniqueness under the stated finite\nconditions","<p><em> Put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>greedyMersenneSupport</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>,\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>. The following are\nthree separate uniqueness statements.</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em>If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∩</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>If <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∩</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>Let positive integer weights <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> for a positive\ninteger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>g</mi></math></span>. For a nonnegative\ninteger target <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>T</mi></math></span>, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></math></span> be the word obtained by visiting\nthese weights in order and taking each when it fits. An admissible\nBoolean word <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></span> has <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>g</mi></math></span> if and only if\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>g</mi></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>Part (iii) gives uniqueness under the small-remainder condition,\nnot existence. Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-i11a\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-i11a\">6.100</a> gives a\none-weight counterexample to dropping that condition.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#lem:collapse-mech","Carry and residual value","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>∉</mo><mi>A</mi></math></span>, put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>δ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math></span>, and let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ihc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> denote the\ninteger half-carry at level <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span>. Then\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>ihc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>δ</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>+</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>≤</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>≤</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em>\nwhere <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#prop:collapse","A cofinal carry bound","<p><em> If\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>ihc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></math></span> for arbitrarily large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span>, with fixed constants <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. For the particular greedy\nsupport <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi></math></span> of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, a one-sided upper bound <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ihc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></math></span> already suffices.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#lem:sqrt-witness","The terminal bound at square depths","<p><em>\nSuppose <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>∉</mo><mi>A</mi></math></span>. Then for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>ihc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>≤</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#prop:collapsed-list","Six equivalent membership\nconditions","<p><em> Each of the following is logically <em>equivalent</em>\nto <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span>, not\nstrictly weaker:</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em><span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span> for\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>;</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>there are arbitrarily large positive exponents outside <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>G</mi></math></span>;</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>at arbitrarily large depths <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>, some <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> satisfies <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>; no agreement between\nthe sets <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi></math></span> at different depths is\nrequired;</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>at arbitrarily large <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi></math></span>,\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ihc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>;</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>at arbitrarily large positive depths <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi></math></span>, some <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> satisfies <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>ihc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>;</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>the half-target greedy remainder never exceeds the full\nremaining tail, so no finite fatal gap exists; the seven equivalent\nforms in the later classification express this same\ncondition.</em></p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>For (d) and (e), the reverse directions use the square depths in\nLemma <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#lem:sqrt-witness\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#lem:sqrt-witness\">2.6</a>. For\n(a), membership gives <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span> when\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. The forward implication still\nneeds the greedy inequality <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#prop:local-void","Limits of the specified local\nsummaries","<p><em> (i) After <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi></math></span> common\nsteps the endpoint residue mod <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup></math></span>\nof an affine binary orbit is <em>independent</em> of the initial carry:\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. (ii)\nFix <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo></math></span>. Consider the\ncoefficient sequences </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Their binary sums\nare all <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>, and their scaled\ntails before position <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span> agree, but\ntheir scaled tails immediately after <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span> are <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi></math></span>. Thus any exact label-and-decoder\nsystem recovering those latter tails must have at least <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> labels. A\nstate determined only by the common preceding history, with no new\ninput, cannot distinguish them. (iii) For any starting carry and any\nfinite list of prescribed valuations and odd unit residues modulo <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>u</mi></msup></math></span>, with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>u</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, there are integer input\ncoefficients with those data whose successor carries lie in their\nprescribed centred intervals. The unrestricted higher bits of the input\ncoefficients may be chosen separately at each step, as in\nProposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#prop:2adic-nogo\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#prop:2adic-nogo\">10.4</a>,\nso these fixed-precision symbols alone do not exclude a completion in\nthat specified family. This says nothing about extra constraints imposed\nby divisor counts from one common support.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#prop:exponent-gap","A bound for the reduced\ndenominator","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, let\n<span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>Skip</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>,\nand let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> be the reduced\ndenominator of the associated finite sum. Since <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> divides the product of its Mersenne\ndenominators, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Skip</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Skip</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The middle\ninequality is strict when the skip set is nonempty; for an empty skip\nset both sums are zero. This is an upper bound, not a quadratic\nasymptotic for <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>. Combined with\nthe cited fixed irrationality-measure exponent, it does not supply the\nrequired <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>-scale estimate.\nEven an asymptotic for the exponent sum would need additional\ninformation about the skip distribution.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:one-sided","One-sidedness","<p><em> Non-membership of\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> in <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span> has an effectively checkable\nfinite-certificate formulation, hence a <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup></math></span> formulation. Membership has\nthe complementary <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Π</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup></math></span>\nformulation. Survival through a tested finite depth alone does not\nestablish membership; a uniform theorem or inductive invariant could.\nThe arithmetical-hierarchy form by itself proves neither undecidability\nnor the absence of finite proofs.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:full-support","Full-support irrationality,\nunconditional, every base <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>","<p><em> For every integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>,\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>is irrational.</mtext></math></span></div>\n<p><em> <strong>Hypotheses:</strong> <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>. <strong>Conclusion:</strong>\nunconditional irrationality of the full-support Erdős–Borwein-type\nseries at every base, not merely base <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn></math></span>. The base-<span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn></math></span> instance recovering the classical\nErdős–Borwein constant’s irrationality is a one-line corollary.</em></p>"]],"source":"erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.json?v=d132333b629d"}
